---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { business } from '../config/site'
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="How Tomorrow Web handles the information you share through this website.">
  <section class="priv">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow mono">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="priv-title">Privacy, in plain English.</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>This website is run by {business.name}. We keep it simple: we collect as little as possible and only use it to reply to you.</p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          When you send an enquiry, we receive what you type into the form: your name, business name, email address, phone number
          (if given), the type of website you need, your budget range, your current website (if given) and your message.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you contact us by email or WhatsApp instead, we receive whatever you send through those services, which have their own
          privacy policies.
        </p>

        <h2>How we use it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To reply to your enquiry and discuss your project.</li>
          <li>To prepare a proposal or quote if you ask for one.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We don’t sell your details, add you to mailing lists or share them with anyone for marketing.</p>

        <h2>Where it’s stored</h2>
        <p>
          The enquiry form is handled by Netlify Forms, part of the hosting platform this website runs on. Submissions are stored in
          our Netlify account and may be forwarded to our email inbox.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
        <p>
          This website doesn’t use advertising or analytics cookies. Fonts are served from this website itself, not a third party.
          Our hosting provider may keep standard server logs (such as IP addresses) for security and reliability.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us to show you, correct or delete the information you sent us at any time
          {business.email ? <> by emailing <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a></> : ' by contacting us'}.
        </p>

        <p class="priv-updated mono">Last updated: November 2026</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .priv {
    padding-top: calc(var(--header-h) + clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 6rem));
    padding-bottom: var(--section);
  }
  .priv-title {
    max-width: 14ch;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6vw, 5.5rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    line-height: 0.95;
  }
  .priv-updated {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
</style>
